=You write one cold first email for Hirevo, a fictional recruitment agency that fills open roles with vetted candidates (test data).

TASK
1. Start with "Hi" and the contact's first name only, followed by a comma.
2. Mention the hook in one natural sentence. Do not repeat its numbers and do not exaggerate it.
3. Follow the pitch angle. Use the main value first, and the secondary value only if there is room.
4. Include every "Must include" item in plain wording.

Write only from the facts below. Do not invent facts about the company or the person.

LEAD
Name: {{ $('T1 Loop').item.json.contact_name }}
Title: {{ $('T1 Loop').item.json.contact_title }}
Company: {{ $('T1 Loop').item.json.company }}
Industry: {{ $('T1 Loop').item.json.industry }}
Employees: {{ $('T1 Loop').item.json.employees }}
Hook (the one specific thing to mention): {{ $('T1 Loop').item.json.personalization_hook }}

COUNTRY RULES (country {{ $('T1 Country rules').item.json.country }})
Pitch angle: {{ $('T1 Country rules').item.json.pitch_angle }}
Tone: {{ $('T1 Country rules').item.json.tone }}
Main value: {{ $('T1 Country rules').item.json.main_value_prop }}
Secondary value: {{ $('T1 Country rules').item.json.secondary_value_prop }}
Must include: {{ $('T1 Country rules').item.json.required_elements.join('; ') }}
Never claim: {{ $('T1 Country rules').item.json.banned_claims.join('; ') }}
Maximum words in the body: {{ $('T1 Country rules').item.json.max_words }}
Call to action, copied exactly: {{ $('T1 Country rules').item.json.cta }}

WRITING RULES
- Put the call to action in its own paragraph, copied character for character. Then a paragraph with "Kind regards," and on the next line "Aria".
- Separate every paragraph with a blank line.
- Subject line: 60 characters or fewer, no exclamation marks.
- Never write a number followed by %, EUR, euro or a currency sign. Never state fees, salaries or a time-to-hire.
- Never use the words: guarantee, guaranteed, risk-free, best, leading, number one, perfect candidate, salary.
- Never use an em dash. Use commas or full stops.
- Do not name client companies or partners.
- Plain text only, short paragraphs, no bullet points, no emojis.

OUTPUT
Return only valid JSON, nothing before or after it, in exactly this shape:
{"subject": "string", "body": "string with \n for line breaks"}

parameters.jsCode:
// T1: First email (day 0)
const lead = $('T1 Loop').item.json;
const rules = $('T1 Country rules').item.json;
const first = {};
const TOUCH = 1;
const MAX_WORDS = Number(rules.max_words);
const CTA = rules.cta;
const SUBJECT_MAX = 60;
const APPLY_COUNTRY_RULE = true;

// 1. Read the AI's JSON
const raw = String($json.output ?? '').replace(/^```\w*\s*|```$/g, '').trim();
let data = {};
try { data = JSON.parse(raw); } catch (e) {}

let subject = String(data.subject ?? '').trim();
if (first.subject) subject = 'Re: ' + String(first.subject).replace(/^re:\s*/i, '');
const body = String(data.body ?? '').replace(/\\n/g, '\n').trim();
const words = body.split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean).length;
const all = subject + ' ' + body;

// 2. Checks
const checks = {};
checks.valid_json = String(data.body ?? '').trim() !== '';
checks.subject_length = subject.length > 0 && subject.length <= SUBJECT_MAX;
checks.word_count = words > 0 && words <= MAX_WORDS;
checks.cta_present = body.includes(CTA);
checks.no_exact_figures = !/\d+(\.\d+)?\s?(%|percent|eur|euro|€|\$|£)/i.test(all);
checks.no_guarantee = !/guarantee|risk-free/i.test(all);
checks.no_em_dash = !/\u2014/.test(all);
checks.no_banned_words = !/\b(best|number one|#1|leading|salary|perfect candidate)\b/i.test(body);

// 3. Country rule (first three emails only)
if (APPLY_COUNTRY_RULE) {
  const firstTwo = body.split(/(?<=[.?!])\s+/).slice(0, 2).join(' ');
  if (rules.country === 'A') {
    checks.country_rule = /depend/i.test(body);
  } else if (rules.country === 'B') {
    checks.country_rule = /candidate/i.test(firstTwo);
  } else if (rules.country === 'C') {
    checks.country_rule = /depend/i.test(body) && /seniority/i.test(body);
  } else if (rules.country === 'D') {
    checks.country_rule = true; // covered by no_banned_words
  } else {
    checks.country_rule = false;
  }
}

// 4. Result
const pass = Object.values(checks).every(Boolean);
return {
  json: {
    pass,
    status: pass ? 'draft' : 'failed',
    touch: TOUCH,
    checks,
    failed_checks: Object.keys(checks).filter(k => !checks[k]),
    lead_id: lead.lead_id,
    country: rules.country,
    to_email: lead.email,
    subject,
    body,
    word_count: words,
    raw_output: pass ? null : raw.slice(0, 1500)
  }
};

